{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_whk4gkpcskftef5vywczj77ell5vdecfrd5ltisozqccugmorrza","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 10 tests pass cleanly. Summary of what I did:\n\n## Phase 1 — Translation (`src/ljmm.rs`)\n\nThe C library is a `mmap64` wrapper that reserves the [sbrk(0), 2G] address range for the process and tries to satisfy `MAP_32BIT` allocations from a best-fit hole found by parsing `/proc/self/maps`. The Rust public API only exposes three functions (`ljmm_init`, `ljmm_let_os_take_care_1g_2g`, `ljmm_test_set_test_param`) — none of the wrapper/parsing internals. I implemented these as safe Rust over a single `Mutex`-guarded global state struct that mirrors the C `ljmm_t`:\n\n- `ljmm_init()` populates defaults exactly like the C constructor (page size 4096, `addr_upbound = 0x80000000`, `os_take_care_1g_2g = 1` matching the non-`STRESS_TEST` build, `map_file = \"/proc/self/maps\"`, 8192-byte buffer) and returns `1`.\n- `ljmm_let_os_take_care_1g_2g(turn_on)` truncates to a `i8` to match the C `char` field's narrowing assignment.\n- `ljmm_test_set_test_param(...)` updates `map_file`, `addr_lowbound`, `page_size`, and `page_mask`, with a `debug_assert!` that mirrors the C `DEBUG`-only `ASSERT` for power-of-two page size.\n\nI also added `#[doc(hidden)]` `_test_get_*` inspectors so behavior could be verified without `unsafe`/FFI.\n\n## Phase 2 — Tests (`src/bin/test_ljmm.rs`)\n\n10 `#[test]` functions, all serialized with a `Mutex` to avoid races on shared global state. Expected values were probed from a small C program (`page_size=4096`, `ADDR_2G=0x80000000`) and from the C constants in `ljmm.c`. Tests cover: init return code, full default state after init, on/off toggling, char-truncation behavior, multiple test-param invocations with different page sizes, map-file replacement, and that re-running init resets everything.\n\nAll 10 tests pass."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":587,"cache_read_input_tokens":32592,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":587,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c47c5467-277f-4fc3-8b01-53d23d66f75a","uuid":"ca36a4c8-7635-4635-a64f-55dd90a35a88"}
